---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';

// Served straight from this repo's asset-library/ archive (already
// committed on main) via raw.githubusercontent.com, rather than
// Squarespace's CDN. asset-library/ isn't wired into the Astro build,
// so this is a stopgap -- ideally this becomes a self-hosted copy in
// public/case-studies/ (or a proper CDN in front of the repo) later.
const heroImage = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/brianjensen-rdc/rdc-website/main/asset-library/thumbnails_visual-studio-ide-campaign.png';

const meta = [
  { label: 'Company', value: 'Microsoft' },
  { label: 'Asset types', value: 'Video, eBook, presentation, illustration, infographics' },
  { label: 'Services used', value: 'Brand strategy, digital marketing, content marketing, social media marketing, video marketing, graphic design, event marketing' },
];

const results = [
  'Updated presentation decks with refreshed messaging',
  'Custom infographics to visualize and explain complex subscription benefits',
  'Social media content and advertising',
  'Conference booth materials for VSLive! events',
  'Engaging promotional videos that demonstrated the breadth of VSS benefits',
];

const gallery = [
  { src: 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/brianjensen-rdc/rdc-website/main/asset-library/VSS%20Twitter%20Banner.png', alt: 'VSS Twitter banner social graphic', caption: 'Social media: VSS Twitter banner' },
  { src: 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/brianjensen-rdc/rdc-website/main/asset-library/Q4_VSS%20Social_Ad2_VSLive.png', alt: 'VSLive conference social ad for VSS', caption: 'Conference materials: VSLive social ad' },
  { src: 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/brianjensen-rdc/rdc-website/main/asset-library/MICROSOCF%20VSS%20%28A4%20SIZE%29%20FA%20%28DIGITAL%29_Page_1.png', alt: 'VSS benefits one-pager print collateral', caption: 'Print collateral: VSS benefits one-pager' },
];
---
<Layout title="VSS Benefits" description="How Red Door Collaborative helped Microsoft close the communication gap on Visual Studio Subscription benefits.">
  <section class="hero tight">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Case study &middot; Microsoft</span>
      <h1>VSS Benefits campaign.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container">
      <img src={heroImage} alt="Illustration of a laptop with developer tooling icons, representing the Visual Studio Subscriptions benefits campaign" class="case-hero-image" width="900" height="900" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        {meta.map((m) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3>{m.label}</h3>
            <p>{m.value}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Significant market headwinds</span>
      <h2>Closing a communication gap on enterprise benefits.</h2>
      <p>Microsoft's Visual Studio is an integrated developer environment (IDE) that software developers use to write, edit, and build code. However, customers who purchased a Visual Studio subscription (VSS) found that their decision was far from simple: with multiple subscription options and different enterprise-level benefits, many customers were using VSS without accessing their unique benefits. Additionally, the VSS customer base was increasingly migrating to its free, browser-based option, VS Code.</p>
      <p>With the help of our team of embedded consultants already working within VSS, we developed a plan to close a significant communication gap about the benefits included with enterprise-level subscriptions, and create updated marketing materials to communicate the VSS value proposition to administrators and developers alike.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">A holistic approach</span>
      <h2>A top-to-bottom transformation of the VSS marketing presence.</h2>
      <p>We began this project as learners. Working with our own VSS embedded consultants and the creative team, we set out to learn their marketing and messaging challenges, which included a comprehensive review of current marketing assets.</p>
      <p>We then worked closely with the client to develop a messaging and positioning framework that established a consistent tone, style, and voice. The result was a top to bottom transformation of the VSS marketing presence including:</p>
      <div class="tag-list">
        {results.map((r) => <span class="tag">{r}</span>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Selected assets</span>
      <h2>A closer look at the work.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        {gallery.map((g) => (
          <figure class="asset-card">
            <img src={g.src} alt={g.alt} loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>{g.caption}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container">
      <blockquote class="quote">
        Measurable results.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="quote-attribution">The VSS brand refresh not only updated messaging and positioning guidelines, but it also clarified market confusion of VSS's own product line. Red Door played a key role by helping VSS scale their marketing campaigns and encourage customers to take advantage of all the benefits a Visual Studio Subscription offers.</p>
      <p>The result was an uptick in engagement across social media and a clearer messaging model that prepared VSS to thrive in a competitive business landscape.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection heading="Let's collaborate." />
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-hero-image {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 480px;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .asset-card {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--color-bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .asset-card img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 220px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  .asset-card figcaption {
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
